<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">17 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 17 November, from 887 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-fat" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-the-fat.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/887">887 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,139 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles the Fat is deposed at an assembly in Frankfurt</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Frankish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnates</a> deposed Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-fat">Charles the Fat</a>, the last Carolingian to rule a united kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Franks</a>, at an assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>. His nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-of-carinthia">Arnulf of Carinthia</a> became king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a>, and the empire fragmented permanently.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-fat">Charles the Fat</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnulf-of-carinthia">Arnulf of Carinthia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-francia">East Francia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1292">1292 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">734 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Balliol is chosen King of Scots over Robert de Brus</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Noblemen headed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-i-of-england">Edward I of England</a> chose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-balliol">John Balliol</a> as King of Scots over Robert de Brus, ending the succession dispute known as the Great Cause. Balliol was deposed after the English invasion of 1296.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-balliol">John Balliol</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1558">1558 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">468 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Elizabeth I becomes queen of England</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the death of her half-sister Mary I, the 25-year-old Elizabeth succeeded to the throne. Her 44-year reign brought a Protestant church settlement, the defeat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a> and a flowering of literature.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spanish-armada">Spanish Armada</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1592">1592 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">434 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sigismund III Vasa succeeds his father John III as king of Sweden</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-iii-vasa">Sigismund III Vasa</a>, king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> and grand duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a> since 1587, succeeded his father John III as King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. A zealous Catholic, he ruled Sweden until he was deposed in 1599.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismund-iii-vasa">Sigismund III Vasa</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-iii-of-sweden">John III of Sweden</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1869">1869 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">157 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Suez Canal opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Empress Eugénie of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> led a procession of ships through the new canal linking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a>. It cut thousands of kilometres from the sea route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1970">1970 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">56 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Luna 17 lands Lunokhod 1 on the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Soviet Luna 17 landed in the Sea of Rains and released Lunokhod 1, the first remote-controlled rover on another world. Driven from Earth, it travelled about 10 kilometres over ten months.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1973">1973 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">53 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Greek troops crush the Athens Polytechnic uprising</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A tank broke through the gates of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> Polytechnic, ending a student occupation against the military junta. Dozens were killed, and the junta fell the following summer.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Police attack students in Prague, sparking the Velvet Revolution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Riot police beat students at a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> march marking the anniversary of a Nazi crackdown. Outrage fuelled mass protests that ended communist rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> within six weeks.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a></div></div></li></ol>
